  "limits": [
    "SETTINGS generator, ordering and lifetime are pinned public-source facts. Aggregate original capture predicates corroborate its SETTINGS range/logging and once-per-session behavior; this tool does not execute Chromium or decompile it.",
    "Original NetLog JSON dictionary order is not wire-order evidence. Ascending serialization order comes separately from the pinned public encoder.",
    "Observed range/congruence, signed logging, uniqueness and once-per-session counts corroborate this source path but do not prove RNG entropy or independence statistically.",
    "The pinned Chromium DEPS establishes the public GoogleQUICHE association; undocumented Spotify/CEF source patches and arbitrary feature overrides are not excluded by these files alone.",
    "SETTINGS range/congruence and logging have original capture corroboration. The subsequent control-frame generator, payload-length correlation, sequence and lifetime are public-source-only facts; no capture observation of its actual frame or payload bytes is claimed.",
    "The capture catalog has only an unknown-frame RECEIVED event. Outgoing QUIC stream-frame metadata supplies offsets/lengths/FIN, not payload bytes or HTTP3 frame boundaries; no GREASE-frame values or packetization are inferred from it.",
    "Other QUIC/TLS GREASE, packetization and connection fingerprints remain separate.",
    "No current Dart implementation supplies expected values. No app, account, profile, debugger or process is used; optional downloads contact only pinned public source URLs.",
    "Actual original random protocol identifiers/values and their hashes are deliberately omitted, including observed minima/maxima."
  ]
